1	/**
2	 * File-Share Grant Re-Mint on Scope-Exit Rotation (recipient-pin-lifecycle §5)
3	 *
4	 * Proves the web INLINE grant-remint seam: when an owner scope-exit-rotates a
5	 * folder that CONTAINS a separately-shared FILE leaf, the file recipient's grant
6	 * must be re-minted under the file's freshly-rotated read key. The login/
7	 * opportunistic reconcile sweep can NEVER reach a file leaf (a file has no
8	 * FolderTree entry, so the sweep skips it) — only the inline seam
9	 * (`RotationClientCallbacks.resolveInlineGrantRemint` → `rotateReadFromNode`'s
10	 * per-node `reMintGrantsRootedAt`) re-wraps a file grant.
11	 *
12	 * Alice (owner) is wired WITH the inline-grant-remint seam; bob (folder
13	 * recipient, pinned) and carol (file recipient, pin-exempt) receive shares.
14	 * Rotating alice's folder D via a covered mutation (rename) must re-mint BOTH
15	 * grants under the rotated keys.
16	 *
17	 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
18	 * STATUS: describe.skip — this suite is a live-stack REPRODUCTION, not a passing
19	 * gate. Run against a local stack (see repo docs) to reproduce. It surfaced
20	 * three genuine gaps that stop the just-committed fix (04198f81e) from re-minting
21	 * a file grant end-to-end. Two of them are product bugs OUTSIDE tests/sdk-e2e and
22	 * were therefore left unfixed here (this task is test-only). Un-skip once B and C
23	 * below are fixed.
24	 *
25	 *   Gap A (harness artifact, worked around):
26	 *     `client.getRecipientPubkeyPins(D)` slow-paths through
27	 *     getWriteBodyParams → re-resolve → unsealNode when the folder's in-memory
28	 *     `metadata.writeBody` mirror is null (a folder created THIS session via
29	 *     createFolder registers with metadata: null — registerFolder, client.ts).
30	 *     During rotation the published node is already re-sealed under the NEW read
31	 *     key but the in-memory folderKey is still OLD → "CryptoError: Decryption
32	 *     failed" (write-body-params.ts:97). Real-web navigation loads the folder via
33	 *     DFS with metadata populated (fast in-memory pin path), so this is a harness
34	 *     seeding artifact — worked around below by evicting root+D and reloading via
35	 *     ensureFolderLoaded (mirrors a cold navigation). It COULD still bite a
36	 *     same-session create+share+rotate web flow.
37	 *
38	 *   Gap C (REAL product bug — blocks ALL re-mints, folder AND file):
39	 *     sdk-core `reMintGrantsRootedAt` encodes the re-wrapped key as BASE64
40	 *     (`bytesToBase64`, packages/sdk-core/src/rotation/engine.ts:648) and hands it
41	 *     to the host `updateGrantFn`. But `PATCH /shares/:id/grant`
42	 *     (UpdateGrantDto.encryptedReadKey) — like the share-CREATE DTO and the SDK's
43	 *     own share-create path (share/index.ts:71 bytesToHex) — requires even-length
44	 *     HEX. So every re-mint PATCH is rejected:
45	 *       "encryptedReadKey must be an even-length hex string" (400).
46	 *     This affects the WEB owner-reconcile path too (owner-reconcile.service.ts
47	 *     updateGrant passes the base64 verbatim to sharesControllerUpdateGrant). No
48	 *     existing sdk-e2e exercised a real re-mint PATCH, so it was uncaught. Fix:
49	 *     engine.ts:648 should emit `bytesToHex`, or the API/host must agree on
50	 *     base64. The harness exposes an OPT-IN diagnostic (`E2E_REMINT_HEX=1`) that
51	 *     converts base64→hex before the PATCH so this suite can reach Gap B; it is a
52	 *     diagnostic, NOT a fix, and defaults OFF (faithful to web).
53	 *
54	 *   Gap B (REAL product gap — the pitfall this e2e was built to find):
55	 *     Re-minting carol's FILE grant requires the file node F to be rotated (its
56	 *     readKey changes). But `rotateReadFromNode`'s per-node key source
57	 *     (`nodeKeySource`, client.ts) reads ONLY the in-memory `folderTree`, which
58	 *     holds FOLDERS only — a file leaf is never registered there. So rotateOne
59	 *     fail-closes at the D-01 guard (engine.ts:1095):
60	 *       "rotateOne: no valid IPNS private key for k51… — provide via
61	 *        nodeKeySource (Phase 64) or write-body wiring (Phase 65)".
62	 *     The web fix wires the inline re-mint SEAM but does NOT thread a file leaf's
63	 *     IPNS/write key material into the rotation walk, so a file grant can never be
64	 *     re-minted. The web fix needs to thread file write-material (recover the
65	 *     file's ipnsPrivateKey/writeKey from the parent's write-body) into
66	 *     nodeKeySource, mirroring the desktop/Rust path.
67	 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
68	 */
69	
70	import { describe, it, expect, beforeAll, afterAll } from 'vitest';
71	import { wrapKey, unwrapKey, bytesToHex, hexToBytes } from '@cipherbox/crypto';
72	import { createMultiAccountFixture, type MultiAccountFixture } from '../fixtures/multi-account';
73	import { API_URL, testFetch } from '../fixtures/test-harness';
74	import { generateTextContent } from '../helpers/data-generators';
